  "key": "SFCC-703",
  "summary": "PDP – Maximum Purchase Quantity Override by Customer Group and SKU",
  "description": "As a Site Merchandiser, I want to configure a maximum purchase quantity at the customer group and/or SKU level, so that I can restrict specific customers or specific products to a tighter purchase limit than the global default.\n\nCustomer group limits exist to further restrict certain shoppers — for example, customers identified as resellers may be placed in a customer group with a limit of 1, preventing bulk purchasing. The intent is always to restrict below the global default, not to grant higher limits. The most specific level takes priority: SKU limit → Customer Group limit → Global default.",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
