em reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\" with an info icon  (see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795|smart-link] )\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then a page-level warning banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag has reached maximum quantity\" (see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404|smart-link] )\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the button remains enabled — the auto-cap resolves the quantity issue and checkout is not blocked. Apple Pay and Google Pay express buttons also remain enabled."
